# FirefoxChatImprover — feature status / TODO

**Baseline audited:** Phase 65 v0.41.6 (2026-08-08)  
**Authoritative release inventory:** `PROJECT_STATUS.md`  
**Patch Tool public contract:** v6.7.9 (`tools/_patch_lib/docs/AI_USAGE_CONTRACT.md`, `PORTABLE_USAGE.md`)

This file previously contained the Phase 28 v0.28.19 audit. That snapshot is obsolete and incorrectly listed later-completed features as unfinished. The table below is reconciled against the current source and regression inventory.

## 1. Active implementation

No feature is currently in active implementation after Phase 65.

Phase 65 completed the two requested status refinements:

- ready/matched display is compacted to `RD` / `⚠ RD`;
- managed download has an independent header indicator (`⇩` while downloading/moving, `✓` after verified completion).

## 2. Completed items that the old audit incorrectly marked unfinished

| Item from old v0.28.19 audit | Current state | Evidence/baseline |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Restart recovery for managed downloads | **Complete** | Armed captures resume while valid; relocation is recovered through idempotent Native Host move receipts. |
| Native Host for Windows | **Complete** | Windows install/uninstall, registry registration, execution, process-tree stop and integration tooling are present. |
| Native log cleanup policy | **Complete** | Native Host 0.13.0 includes bounded age/size/file-count retention controls. |
| Real Firefox E2E | **Complete** | Opt-in real-Firefox runner covers tab/title/badge/DOM/navigation and optional Native Host flow. |
| Firefox version matrix | **Complete** | Matrix runner emits JSON/Markdown results per configured Firefox binary. |
| Firefox Android manifest compatibility | **Complete** | Minimum Firefox 142 resolves the previous manifest warning. |
| Search/filter | **Complete** | Tabs, profiles, presets and command history are filtered non-destructively. |
| Named working sessions | **Complete** | Searchable session catalog with save/update/rename/duplicate/delete/import/export. |
| Optional sound alerts | **Complete** | Per-profile/tab bounded sound alert, default off. |
| Trusted-URL auto activation | **Complete** | Opt-in and permission-gated. |
| Per-rule statistics | **Complete** | Session-isolated counters/timings/export/reset. |
| Per-run compressed logs | **Complete** | ZIP export with full transcript/metadata/fallback completeness. |
| Chromium port | **Complete** | Chrome/Edge MV3 package and Native Host registration flow. |
| Accessibility audit | **Complete** | Keyboard/focus/screen-reader/contrast/reduced-motion coverage. |

## 3. Not code-in-progress

| Item | Classification | Reason |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Self-hosted persistent Firefox update channel | **Operator dependency** | Code/tooling is complete; activation requires a Mozilla-signed XPI, stable HTTPS URLs and deployment credentials. |
| Pre-v0.28.20 command log bytes already deleted from disk | **Physical limitation** | Metadata can be rediscovered, but deleted historical bytes cannot be reconstructed. |
| Native Host for macOS | **Deferred** | Explicitly excluded from the current implementation sequence by project decision. |

## 4. Patch Tool v6.7.9 integration rules

- Normal user command is only `./tools/run_python_patches.sh`.
- AI COLLECT requests are delivered as one ZIP containing exactly one `CODE_COLLECTION_REQUEST*.json`; loose request JSON is rejected.
- PATCH execution through the public launcher is in-place (`--transaction off`); SANDBOX/detached-worktree workflow is removed.
- Readonly COLLECT remains non-transactional and successful COLLECT output highlights the result ZIP once.

## 5. Remaining Patch Tool v6.7.9 status items

These belong to the Patch Tool itself, not the FirefoxChatImprover feature backlog:

- exact replacement of private installed core modules: **not claimed** because exact current private-core source was not part of the v6.7.9 release input;
- unified pre-selector identity/history/duplicate filtering: **private-core dependent**;
- exact LAST_RUN synthesis for dispatcher-only delete/cancel/not-selected events: **private-core dependent**;
- real large-project COLLECT validation: **pending user runtime evidence**;
- phase-inference refinement: **deferred unless real COLLECT output demonstrates weak markers**.
